BEGIN:VCALENDAR
VERSION:2.0
PRODID:-//WebMS Intra//Test fixture//EN
X-WEBMS-FIXTURE-NOTE:What this proves: a CANCELLED series cancels its changed dates too, even when
X-WEBMS-FIXTURE-NOTE:the changed date says STATUS:CONFIRMED. cancelled-series.ics has no changed
X-WEBMS-FIXTURE-NOTE:date in it, so it cannot show this. All three dates must come back cancelled.
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:cancelled-with-override-1@fixtures.webms.test
DTSTAMP:20260901T090000Z
DTSTART;TZID=Europe/London:20261201T190000
DTEND;TZID=Europe/London:20261201T200000
RRULE:FREQ=WEEKLY;COUNT=3
STATUS:CANCELLED
SUMMARY:Cancelled series with a changed date
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:cancelled-with-override-1@fixtures.webms.test
DTSTAMP:20260901T090000Z
RECURRENCE-ID;TZID=Europe/London:20261208T190000
DTSTART;TZID=Europe/London:20261208T200000
DTEND;TZID=Europe/London:20261208T210000
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Cancelled series with a changed date (moved)
END:VEVENT
END:VCALENDAR
